   105	## 2. There is at most one multiple fibre
   106	
   107	The composite
   108	
   109	```text
   110	h=rho o g1:A2->A1
   111	```
   112	
   113	is a nonconstant polynomial.  Choose a general affine line `L subset A2` on
   114	which `h` is nonconstant.  Then `g1|L:A1->U` is a nonconstant curve transverse
   115	to `rho`.
   116	
   117	Miyanishi Lemma 1.4.16 says that an `A1`-fibration over `A1` with at least
   118	two multiple fibres admits no such transverse morphism from `A1`.  Its proof
   119	is the exact polynomial-power obstruction: over two multiple values one gets
   120	
   121	```text
   122	p(s)^a-q(s)^b=constant,       a,b>=2,
   123	```
   124	
   125	and factorization/Mason--Stothers (equivalently the positive-genus
   126	superelliptic curve after removing the common gcd) makes both polynomials
   127	constant.  Therefore `rho` has at most one multiple fibre.
   128	
   129	The use of a general source line is essential.  No assertion that `g1`
   130	preserves the ruling, is finite, or maps a generic source fibre to a ruling
   131	fibre is made.
