   133	## 3. The no-multiple row is impossible
   134	
   135	If there is no multiple fibre, every scheme fibre is a smooth `A1`.  The
   136	equidimensional morphism from the smooth surface to the smooth curve is flat,
   137	hence smooth.  It is an `A1`-bundle.  Over `A1`, its line-bundle and additive
   138	torsor classes vanish (`Pic(A1)=H^1(A1,O)=0`), so
   139	
   140	```text
   141	U isomorphic to A2.                                           (3.1)
   142	```
   143	
   144	Under (3.1), `pi:U->A2` becomes a polynomial Keller self-map of geometric
   145	degree three.  Orevkov Theorem 1.1 excludes polynomial maps of `C2` with
   146	nonzero constant Jacobian and geometric degree two or three.  Hence the
   147	no-multiple row is empty.
