   162	### 4.1 Missed divisors and the cofinite image
   163	
   164	Let `V=g1(A2)`, an open subset of `U`.  The free group on the prime divisors
   165	contained in `U minus V` injects into `Pic(U)`.  Indeed, if a rational
   166	function `b` has divisor supported there, then `b` and `b^-1` are regular on
   167	the normal open `V`.  Their pullbacks are mutually inverse polynomials on
   168	`A2`, hence scalars.  Dominance makes `b` the same scalar, so its divisor was
   169	zero.  This proves linear independence of all missed prime divisors.
   170	
   171	The finite group (4.1) contains no nonzero free subgroup.  Thus `U minus V`
   172	has no curve component.  It is a finite set:
