    68	## 2. Direct reconstruction
    69	
    70	The binding block theorem gives `Y` integral, normal, affine, and finite over
    71	`A2_C`; hence `Y` is a finite-type excellent complex surface.  It also gives
    72	that `R` is nonempty and pure of codimension one,
    73	`g1(A2) subset Y_sm minus R`, and `Sing(Y) subset R`.
    74	
    75	### 2.1 Affineness and smoothness
    76	
    77	Apply Stacks Project Theorem 58.29.3, Tag `0ECD`, with Stacks-source `Y`,
    78	Stacks-target `A2_C`, and morphism `g2`.  Its literal conclusion is that the
    79	inclusion of the maximal etale open into the normal source is an **affine
    80	morphism**.  The maximal etale open is exactly `U=Y minus R`; since `Y` is
    81	affine, `U` is affine.  One must not shorten the theorem to the false absolute
    82	claim that every such maximal etale open is affine without the affine-source
    83	hypothesis.
    84	
    85	This direct route uses normality of `Y`, finite type of `g2`, and the excellent
    86	regular target over a field.  It does not need dimension two, purity, or
    87	nonemptiness for this affineness step, although those properties remain
    88	promoted block data and enter other block arguments.  The Nagata
    89	normal-excellent-surface divisor-complement theorem supplies an independent
    90	route using purity.
    91	
    92	By definition `g2|U` is etale.  Since its target is smooth, `U` is smooth.
    93	Because `g1(A2)` avoids `R`, `g1` factors uniquely through `U`; density in
    94	`Y` implies density in the nonempty open `U`, and etaleness and
    95	quasi-finiteness are unchanged.
    96	
    97	### 2.2 Units, rationality, and logarithmic Kodaira dimension
    98	
    99	Dominance makes
   100	
   101	```text
   102	g1^*:O(U) -> C[x,y]
   103	```
   104	
   105	injective.  A unit therefore pulls back to a scalar, and injectivity applied
   106	to its difference from that scalar gives `O(U)^*=C^*`.  The finite extension
   107	`C(U) subset C(x,y)` makes `U` unirational; Castelnuovo in characteristic zero
   108	makes its smooth projective model rational.
   109	
   110	For a dominant generically finite morphism of smooth open varieties,
   111	log-pluricanonical pullback gives
   112	
   113	```text
   114	bar-kappa(A2) >= bar-kappa(U).
   115	```
   116	
   117	Since `bar-kappa(A2)=-infinity`, necessarily
   118	`bar-kappa(U)=-infinity`.  Etaleness without properness does not upgrade this
   119	to a general equality theorem; only the displayed direction is consumed.
