   131	whose general scheme fibre is `A1`; no base or field extension is inserted.
   132	Rationality of `U` and Luroth make `C` rational.  Pullback along the
   133	surjective `rho` injects `O(C)^*` into `C^*`, so a smooth rational affine base
   134	has at most one puncture.  Thus `C=A1` or `P1`.  The projective-base branch is
   135	real for general smooth affine surfaces and is not excluded here.
   136	
   137	The charged Gurjar--Miyanishi fibre lemma says that every fibre, after taking
   138	its reduced structure, is a disjoint union of affine lines.  This controls
   139	neither Cartier multiplicities nor the number of bad fibres or components.
   140	
   141	If `q_t` is the number of reduced components at a bad value, Euler additivity
   142	over the complement of the finite bad-value set gives the presentation-free
   143	identity
